# The gap warning in the debug VS match on Final Destination: Link (player
# 1) against Mario (player 2), a human slot with no input, who stands still.
# Link jumps in place over the main floor, where nothing sounds, then runs
# off the left edge and comes back with the midair jump: the gap warning
# starts once he is past the edge and stops a short hold after he is back
# over the floor.
# Run from Git Bash with the debug match switches (the debug match is on
# Final Destination), cues on, and a dump to check the tone's level:
#   MELEE_DEBUG_VS=1 MELEE_DEBUG_VS_STOCKS=2 MELEE_A11Y_CUES=1 \
#     MELEE_A11Y_CUE_DUMP=build/drive/gap.f32 \
#     python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/match_gap.drive
# then grep -c '\[a11y\] cue gap st' build/drive/last.log prints 2: drive.py
# cannot fail on a line too many, which run_level.py checks itself.

# Start on the title screen goes straight into the debug match.
wait "state 0 scene 0$"
press Start until "boot scene: state \d+ scene 2$"

# Both position cues start at GO, Link standing at x = -60.
wait 'cue your position start pan -0\.35 pitch 1\.07 ' 60
sleep 1

# A full jump in place, over the main floor: no gap.
press X 300
sleep 1.2

# A dash off the left edge, the midair jump back towards the stage and
# drifting right onto it. The warning starts past the edge, at x = -86.6
# where the cast stops meeting the floor, and stops on the way back.
press Left 450
wait 'cue gap start pan 0\.00 pitch 1\.00 gain 1\.00$' 5
press X+Right 200
sleep 0.2
press Right 800
wait 'cue gap stop pan 0\.00 pitch 1\.00 gain 1\.00$'
sleep 1.5
